 /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
- * One-shot command submission
+ * Batched command submission
+ *
+ * Every operation used to be one command buffer, submitted and waited on:
+ * a Killzone 2 frame (~1700 draws, plus clears, uploads and snapshots) paid
+ * as many GPU round trips, and the FIFO thread spent most of its time in
+ * vkWaitForFences while the guest waited for the RSX. Operations are now
+ * recorded into one open command buffer, which is submitted and waited on
+ * only when the host needs a result (readbacks, present, the engine's
+ * submit_and_wait) or a per-batch resource runs out:
+ *  - ordering: a full memory barrier opens every operation (all images stay
+ *    in GENERAL), so each one still sees everything recorded before it;
+ *  - per-operation data (vertices, indices, constants, upload staging) is
+ *    suballocated from one host-coherent ring, reset after each wait;
+ *  - each draw gets its own descriptor set from a pool reset after each wait;
+ *  - objects released while the batch is open are destroyed after it ran.
+ * PS3RECOMP_VK_SYNC=1 restores one submission per operation.
